-- Data: the flow control term texts after the streamed tape (card vertex-flow-terms-streamed-tape). The 0081 texts of
-- futures_deep_trades and flow_control_state say that the futures tape is sampled and that the futures side is no_data with
-- the reason sampled_tape. Pull request #328 (migration 0083) streams the ES and NQ tape, computes the futures state from
-- it and removes the reason sampled_tape. Each UPDATE replaces the whole description. Guard: the row still has the 0081
-- text (md5) and no operator mark (edit, certification or certification note); other rows are left alone, so a second
-- run changes nothing. updated_at moves, so a certify call from a page that loaded the old text is refused.
UPDATE "semantic_terms"
SET "description" = 'Futures deep trades: single large trade prints on the futures ES (S&P 500) and NQ (Nasdaq 100). One deep trade is one print at or above the deep-trade size limit of its market; the limit in force is the field limitSize of the tool answer. Unit: contracts. Sign: buy means the print was signed as buyer-initiated, sell as seller-initiated; netVolume is buy volume minus sell volume and is positive when large buying leads. Horizon: the regular session, 09:30 to 16:00 New York; sums start at 09:30. Coverage caveat: the trades come from the streamed tape of the future (field capture: streamed). The field coverage gives the covered seconds of the rule window and their share; a covered second lies between two received prints of a live trade stream. Coverage says that the stream was live; it is not checked against a second source, so it does not prove that no print was lost. A minute without coverage is a gap, not zero. When a part of the session was sampled (field capture: sampled), the sums of that session are lower bounds. Sides come from the quote rule against the quotes of the same contract, else from the tick rule, which follows the last price change; each trade carries its signing method. Vertex has no market-by-order data, so the size of resting orders is not shown. Vertex has no stored query for this term. Call the tool flow_control with group sp500 (ES) or nasdaq100 (NQ) and read deepTrades and futures. The futures state (see flow_control_state) comes from these deep trades. Research input only; not a trade instruction.', "updated_at" = now()
WHERE "id" = 'futures_deep_trades' AND md5("description") = '9cbffc7430fd2c5e74f41631edff955d'
  AND "updated_by" IS NULL AND NOT "certified" AND "certified_at" IS NULL
  AND "certified_by" IS NULL AND "certification_note" IS NULL;
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "semantic_terms"
SET "description" = 'Flow control state: for one index group (sp500: ES futures with SPX and SPY options; nasdaq100: NQ futures with QQQ and NDX options), one state for the options side (from options_net_drift) and one for the futures side (from the deep trades of the streamed futures tape, see futures_deep_trades). States: buyers, sellers, balanced, mixed or no_data; no_data always has a reason (market_closed, source_unavailable, storage_failed, stale, gap, session_start, not_collected). The futures side is never mixed. Its ratio is deep buy volume minus deep sell volume, divided by their sum, over the covered minutes of the window. A futures state starts only when its entry checks pass; the field hold names the first check that failed (few_trades, delta_against or price_against). A gap in the tape ends a futures state. Agreement of the two sides: agree (the same control side), diverge, one_sided, both_balanced or not_comparable (a side is no_data or the options side is mixed); only agree counts as agreement, and it is not tested as an entry rule. Sign: buyers is bullish, sellers is bearish. Unit: none; each side carries its measured ratio and the limit it is compared with, and the fields rules (options) and futuresRules (futures) hold every number of the rules with their version. Horizon: a trailing window inside the regular session, anchored at 09:30 New York; since is the start of the present state. Coverage caveat: the options side is complete for the vendor filter; the futures side uses only the covered minutes of the streamed tape, and its coverage is not checked against a second source. The field study says whether the continuation rule was tested and with what verdict. Vertex has no stored query for this term. Call the tool flow_control with group sp500 or nasdaq100. Read the enums, not the label text. For a no_data side report the reason and do not estimate. A state describes recent flow; it is never a trade instruction.', "updated_at" = now()
WHERE "id" = 'flow_control_state' AND md5("description") = '79911cad1110c678922771aa5c671a98'
  AND "updated_by" IS NULL AND NOT "certified" AND "certified_at" IS NULL
  AND "certified_by" IS NULL AND "certification_note" IS NULL;
